INT. AVALANCHE RESCUE HUT - NIGHT

One room. A woodstove ticking. Bunks bolted to the wall. Snow whispers on the shutters.

INGRID LJUNGBERG, 30s, wool hat, sits cross-legged by the stove feeding it splinters. ALEJANDRO "ALEX" SOTOMAYOR, 20s, sleeping bag to his chin, sips tea and watches her.

A radio on the shelf murmurs low static.

ALEX
It's quiet.

INGRID
Good quiet.

ALEX
Is there another kind?

INGRID
Yes.

The stove pops. Alex smiles faintly. Ingrid tosses another splinter.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Try to sleep.

ALEX
I'm too warm.

INGRID
That's the point of the hut.

He closes his eyes. Opens one.

ALEX
Do you ever get used to it?

INGRID
To what?

ALEX
The mountain. How it just... waits.

Ingrid considers. The wind outside drops a moment.

INGRID
No.

ALEX
Me neither.

He lets his head sink into the pillow. The radio crackles. Both of them look at it.

RANGER PALOMAKI (V.O.)
Hut two, hut two, this is Ranger Palomaki. Do you copy?

Ingrid crosses and picks it up.

INGRID
Palomaki, Ljungberg. Go ahead.

PALOMAKI (V.O.)
Ingrid. How many in the hut?

INGRID
Two. Me and the rookie.

PALOMAKI (V.O.)
Listen to me carefully. The slope above you let go twenty minutes ago.

Ingrid does not move. Alex sits up.

INGRID
Say again.

PALOMAKI (V.O.)
The slide stopped thirty feet short of the hut. Don't open the door.

A deep groan from above. Dust sifts from the rafters. The stove flame leans, then stands upright again.

Alex's eyes find hers. She puts one finger to her lips.
